'''Batliboi Ltd''' is  one of the oldest Indian [[engineering]] companies, founded in 1892.<ref name="Batliboi to issue shares worth 1 bln rupees">{{cite news |date=4 January 2008 |title=Batliboi to issue shares worth 1 bln rupees |url=http://in.reuters.com/article/idINIndia-31244320080104 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160303172912/http://in.reuters.com/article/idINIndia-31244320080104 |archive-date=2016-03-03 |accessdate=24 December 2010 |publisher=Reuters |location=Mumbai}}</ref> The company is involved in [[Machine Tools]], [[Textile]] Air Engineering, Textile Machinery, [[Air Conditioning]], [[Environmental Engineering]],<ref name="TEXT-Fitch rates Batliboi Environmental Engineering 'B+(ind)'">{{cite news |date=21 May 2010 |title=TEXT-Fitch rates Batliboi Environmental Engineering 'B+(ind)' |url=http://in.reuters.com/article/idINWLA468620100521 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304055940/http://in.reuters.com/article/idINWLA468620100521 |archive-date=2016-03-04 |accessdate=24 December 2010 |publisher=Reuters}}</ref> [[Wind Energy]], [[Electrical Engineering]], and International [[Marketing]] and Logistics. Batliboi Ltd. has been registered in [[Bombay Stock Exchange]].{{citation needed|date=October 2018}}

== History ==
It was founded by Jehangir Framji Batliboi. In 1916, the company was acquired by Bhogilal Leherchand, a diamond trader. It went public in 1978.
